thin mouse multiplexing

One thin mouse brain section imaged over sequential RNA and protein staining rounds
on a Nikon spinning-disk confocal (40x/1.3, 0.65 um/px), 4 channels per round
(640, 561, 488, 405 nm). Each file is one channel of a stitched maximum intensity
projection. Stain labels end in RNA (lowercase gene names) or Protein; DAPI = nuclei.
Images are not registered across rounds.
